{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-88239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $-2x{e}^{5x}-3{e}^{5x}\\ge -{x}^{2}{e}^{5x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-88239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x{e}^{5x}-3{e}^{5x} & \\ge -{x}^{2}{e}^{5x} \\\\ {x}^{2}{e}^{5x}-2x{e}^{5x}-3{e}^{5x} & \\ge 0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x-3){e}^{5x} & \\ge 0 \\\\ (x+1)(x-3){e}^{5x} & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${e}^{5x}$ and get\n\n$$\n(x+1)(x-3)\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-1$ and $x=3.$ The parabola is above the $x$-axis when $x\\le -1$ or $x\\ge 3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/assets/6aca0f7c055a5f326c2d0d3bc65b6e68a90c8cb496bc1934dbae6093d0d71f96.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\le -1$ or $x\\ge 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-88239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3305c0a4df184152d8074ed110329cc793fdb009f99b5a73578a208d37b5a33d"} {"question" "q-88239" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-88239" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1\\le x\\le 3"] ["math" "1\\le x\\le 3"] ["math" "x\\ge 3"] ["math" "x\\le -1"] ["text" "$x\\le -1$ or $x\\ge 3$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-88239" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x\\le -1$ or $x\\ge 3$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-88308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $-{9}^{2x-4}{x}^{2}<-5\\cdot {9}^{2x-4}-7\\cdot {9}^{2x-4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-88308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{9}^{2x-4}{x}^{2} & <-5\\cdot {9}^{2x-4}-7\\cdot {9}^{2x-4} \\\\ -{9}^{2x-4}{x}^{2}+5\\cdot {9}^{2x-4}+7\\cdot {9}^{2x-4} & <0 \\\\ (-{x}^{2}+5+7){9}^{2x-4} & <0 \\\\ (12-{x}^{2}){9}^{2x-4} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${9}^{2x-4}$ and solve the resulting inequality using familiar techniques:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12-{x}^{2} & <0 \\\\ -{x}^{2} & <-12 \\\\ {x}^{2} & >12 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & >\\sqrt{12} \\\\ |x| & >2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to the inequality above is $x<-2\\sqrt{3}$ or $x>2\\sqrt{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-88308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3305c0a4df184152d8074ed110329cc793fdb009f99b5a73578a208d37b5a33d"} {"question" "q-88308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-88308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\sqrt{3}<x<2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "x>\\sqrt{3}"] ["text" "$x<-2$ or $x>2$"] ["text" "$x<-2\\sqrt{3}$ or $x>2\\sqrt{3}$"] ["text" "$x<-\\sqrt{3}$ or $x>\\sqrt{3}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-88308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x<-2\\sqrt{3}$ or $x>2\\sqrt{3}$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-278274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality ${x}^{2}\\cdot {9}^{2x-3}\\le {9}^{2x+1}.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\le x$ \n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-278274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {9}^{2x-3} & \\le {9}^{2x+1} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {9}^{2x-3}-{9}^{2x+1} & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {9}^{2x-3}-{9}^{4}\\cdot {9}^{2x-3} & \\le 0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-{9}^{4})\\cdot {9}^{2x-3} & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${9}^{2x-3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{2}-{9}^{4})\\cdot {9}^{2x-3}}{{9}^{2x-3}} & \\le \\frac{0}{{9}^{2x-3}} \\\\ {x}^{2}-{9}^{4} & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{9}^{4} & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\le {9}^{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\le \\sqrt{{9}^{4}} \\\\ |x| & \\le {9}^{2} \\\\ |x| & \\le 81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to the inequality above is $-81\\le x<81.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-278274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3305c0a4df184152d8074ed110329cc793fdb009f99b5a73578a208d37b5a33d"} {"question" "q-278274" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-278274" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-81"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacad