gin{aligned}{x}^{4}\\cdot {4}^{3x-5} & \\ge {4}^{3x-1} \\\\ {x}^{4}\\cdot {4}^{3x-5}-{4}^{3x-1} & \\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{4}\\cdot {4}^{3x-5}-{4}^{4}\\cdot {4}^{3x-5} & \\ge 0 \\\\ ({x}^{4}-{4}^{4}){4}^{3x-5} & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${4}^{3x-5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{4}-{4}^{4}){4}^{3x-5}}{{4}^{3x-5}} & \\ge \\frac{0}{{4}^{3x-5}} \\\\ {x}^{4}-{4}^{4} & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}-{4}^{4} & \\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{4} & \\ge {4}^{4} \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{{x}^{4}} & \\ge \\sqrt[4]{{4}^{4}} \\\\ |x| & \\ge 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality above is  $x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge 4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-278282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3305c0a4df184152d8074ed110329cc793fdb009f99b5a73578a208d37b5a33d"} {"question" "q-278282" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-278282" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-278282" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "valu