 & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${3}^{2x-5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{2}-{3}^{2}){2}^{2x-5}}{{3}^{2x-5}} & \\ge \\frac{0}{{3}^{2x-5}} \\\\ {x}^{2}-{3}^{2} & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{3}^{2} & \\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ge {3}^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{{3}^{2}} \\\\ |x| & \\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality above is  $x\\le -3$ or $x\\ge 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-278284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3305c0a4df184152d8074ed110329cc793fdb009f99b5a73578a208d37b5a33d"} {"question" "q-278284" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-278284" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f5375cf9e104f92020bc303fa9eefd"} {"question" "q-278284" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14036850/state.json" "file_sha256" "518327c45fb02a2f6bb0f2a5f9546f64e7f537